11
00:49:55,384 --> 00:50:01,384
Saturday Night Fever is a 1977 American dance drama film directed
by John Badham and produced by Robert Stigwood.

12
00:54:27,692 --> 00:54:33,692
It stars John Travolta as Tony Manero, a young Italian-American man who spends his weekends dancing and drinking at a local
disco while dealing with social tensions and disillusionment in his working class ethnic neighborhood in Brooklyn.

13
00:59:00,000 --> 00:59:06,000
The story is based on "Tribal Rites of the New Saturday Night", a mostly
fictional 1976 New York article by music writer Nik Cohn.

14
01:03:32,307 --> 01:03:38,307
A major critical and commercial success, Saturday Night Fever had a
tremendous impact on the popular culture of the late 1970s.

15
01:08:04,615 --> 01:08:10,615
It helped popularize disco around the world and initiated a series of
collaborations between film studios and record labels.

16
01:12:36,923 --> 01:12:42,923
It made Travolta, already well known from his role in the popular
TV sitcom Welcome Back, Kotter, a household name.

17
01:17:09,230 --> 01:17:15,230
He was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Actor for his performance, at
the time becoming the fourth-youngest nominee in the category.

18
01:21:41,538 --> 01:21:47,538
The film showcases aspects of the music, dancing, and subculture surrounding the disco era, including
symphony-orchestrated melodies, haute couture styles of clothing, pre-AIDS sexual promiscuity and graceful choreography.

19
01:26:13,846 --> 01:26:19,846
The Saturday Night Fever soundtrack, featuring songs by the Bee Gees,
is one of the best-selling soundtrack albums worldwide.

20
01:30:46,153 --> 01:30:52,153
Travolta reprised his role of Tony Manero in Staying Alive in 1983, which was
panned by critics despite being successful at the box office.

21
01:35:18,461 --> 01:35:24,461
In 2010, Saturday Night Fever was deemed "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant" by the
Library of Congress and selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry.

22
01:39:50,769 --> 01:39:56,769
Adjusted for inflation, it is one of the
highest-grossing R-rated films released in the U.S.

23
01:44:23,076 --> 01:44:29,076
in the 1970s, with a total box office gross of $673,899,098 in 2024.

24
01:48:55,384 --> 01:49:01,384
The film explores themes of dancing master, dance
performance, female lover, disco, lyrical.

25
01:53:27,692 --> 01:53:33,692
The tone is emotional.
